Monograph Introduction: Self-Consistent Stellar Magnetohydrodynamics and Autonomous Energy Conversion Architecture
Thesis
The unification of magnetohydrodynamic (MHD) spectral dynamos with automated Stellar Energy Conversion Units (SECU) and post-quantum cryptographic telemetry pipelines provides a mathematically rigorous framework for simulating stellar interior dynamics and state evolution.
Scope
This monograph formalizes the conversion of continuous mean-field induction PDEs in spherical coordinates into GPU-accelerated Structure of Arrays (SoA) and hybrid Runge-Kutta 4th-order / Backward Differentiation Formulas (BDF2) numerical solvers.
Significance
Authored by independent designer C. Matthew Blackwell, this work establishes reproducible, publication-grade computational architectures that bridge real-world observational astrophysics (Gaia DR3 astrometry, SDSS spectroscopic archives) with secure, fault-tolerant cyber-physical hardware systems.
